// #465, the OTHER arm of the same give-up point in codegen: when codegen cannot
// name the receiver at all it printed a differently-worded diagnostic ("... (no
// type info)") from the same `if`/`else` and likewise emitted nothing. A method
// call on the result of a void function reaches it.
//
// Gated separately from the int/float/bool files because it is the `else` branch,
// not the `if`: a fix applied to only one of the two would leave this one exiting
// 0. Measured before the fix: `wyn check` exit 0, `wyn build` printed the error
// and exit 0. See unknown_method_on_int_rejected.wyn for the full write-up.
// EXPECT_FAIL:
// EXPECT_ERR: (no type info)
fn f() {
    print(1)
}

f().nope_zzz()
